WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:05.220
Arya Stark is one of the most beloved "Game
of Thrones" characters, and one of the few

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.380
to survive all eight seasons.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.969
The youngest Stark daughter has seen more
than her fair share of troubleSs, and audiences

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:16.630
were witness to her cleverness and strength
of will during each adversity.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.810
She was held captive twice, received tortuous
training at the House of Black and White,

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:24.840
and eventually proved her mettle by running
through most of the names on her infamous

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.900
Kill List.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.480
To many fans, it may seem that Arya can do
no wrong — but one would be remiss to say

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.980
that she didn't commit a few sins along the
way.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.920
The character had a tendency to let her emotions
control her actions, as evidenced by her betrayal

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.210
in the House of Black and White, or when she
left the Hound to die in agony.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.830
Yet there is, perhaps, one moment that stands
out above the rest of Arya's transgressions

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:51.230
— one that showed a side of Arya that left
fans with a bitter taste in their mouths.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:55.940
In Season 7, Episode 5 of "Game of Thrones''
— "Eastwatch" — Arya becomes suspicious

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.600
of her sister, Sansa, who appears to be enjoying
her authority a bit too much while Jon Snow

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.289
is away from Winterfell.

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:06.470
Of course, Sansa denies Arya's accusations
that she means to betray their brother, but

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:11.080
when Arya finds the old letter that Sansa
wrote while being held hostage by the Lannisters,

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.700
it seems to cement the younger Stark sister's
doubts.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:18.520
In the very next episode, "Beyond the Wall,"
Sansa sneaks into Arya's room, where she is

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.090
shocked to find Arya's collection of faces.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.780
Arya catches her in the act, and gives her
a bone-chilling, not-so-veiled threat.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.970
When Sansa questions Arya about the faces,
Arya tells her,

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.080
"With the faces, I can choose.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:36.720
I can become someone else — speak in their
voice, live in their skin."

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:43.080
Arya then takes a knife from a table and stalks
closer to Sansa, as she wonders out loud what

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.030
it might be like to wear Sansa's face.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:49.750
Arya then calmly hands Sansa the knife and
walks out of the room, leaving Sansa trembling

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:50.820
in fear.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.430
While it's true that the sisters may not have
gotten along well in the past, the idea of

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.180
Arya threatening Sansa's life is just unsettling,
not to mention out of character.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.420
After all, there are so few members of the
Stark family left, and it would be detrimental

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.220
to their cause if they were to start turning
on each other.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.750
Luckily, Sansa and Arya catch on to Lord Baelish's
scheme to tear them apart, and conduct a scheme

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:12.790
of their own.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.440
Still, Arya definitely had us worried for
a minute.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.350
When you consider the journey Arya goes through
during the entire story of "Game of Thrones,"

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:23.640
it's easy to understand how she could make
a mistake every now and then... especially

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.190
when it comes to trusting people.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:29.810
The tomboy of the highborn, Northern Stark
family, Arya wants nothing more than to learn

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:34.360
to fight and become powerful in her own right,
though her father Ned still holds out hope

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:38.060
that she'll grow up to marry a great lord
and mother plenty of heirs.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.630
Though Arya and Sansa's sisterly squabbles
take up most of the show's first season, the

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:47.150
two are the only witnesses from the family
when Ned is beheaded in King's Landing, and

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.450
years of separation ultimately serve their
relationship.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:55.250
Without her family, Arya goes through a lot,
to put it mildly, constantly escaping captivity

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:00.680
and near-death situations thanks to her quick
instincts, with very few allies to speak of

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.130
— which probably contributes to her trust
issues.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:08.050
Eventually, she befriends the mysterious Jaqen
H'ghar, who leads her to Braavos to teach

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:09.990
her the ways of the Faceless Men.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:14.990
But Arya can't quite follow the Faceless Men's
seemingly endless sets of rules, and uses

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:18.480
her newfound face-shifting abilities to seek
revenge on enemies.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.540
However, it's hard not to root for Arya even
as she shirks the tenets of the Faceless Men;

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.680
the people she decimates are typically purely
evil, like the Stark-murdering Walder Frey,

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.610
making her vengeance feel pretty righteous
in the end.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:35.680
Finally, by Season 8 of the show, Arya seems
to have reached her final form.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:40.040
She uses her fighting skills to destroy The
Night King and save the entire world, survives

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.100
the final struggle for the Iron Throne, and
then blazes her own trail by setting off to

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.420
find what's west of Westeros.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.600
In the end, Arya Stark is what she always
dreamed of being: A powerful, independent

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.150
woman who gets to make her own way in the
world, wherever it might lead her.

